imal move here seems pretty clear.\n\n**Final Play:** I'll lead with the ♣7. It's the cleanest move, maintaining hand structure and giving me flexibility for future plays.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: You are holding two pairs (JJ, 22) and two singles (7, K). Your Pair of 2s is the highest possible pair in the game (as Jokers are singles and Qs cannot form a pair due to cards played). Your Pair of Jacks is also very strong (only beaten by KK, AA, 22). The 7 is your weakest card and a liability.\n\nReason: Leading the single ♣7 is the best strategic move. It removes your lowest card ("trash") immediately, leaving you with a very powerful hand structure (JJ, K, 22). If you were to play the Pair of Jacks first and were forced to use your 22 to regain control, you would be left holding the weak single 7 at the end, which would be difficult to play out. By playing the 7 now, you probe the Landlord\'s hand and maintain high control cards (22) to defend or take the lead later.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣7"]}'}
